From c258b8d69288ed68dd32a13881786750f179fa32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:01:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: huawei_gaokun: Check ucsi->ntfy before
 handling USB events

Since commit 5b4b83c2ffe8 ("usb: typec: ucsi: Set ucsi->connector before
enabling notifications"), ucsi_init() sets ucsi->connector before it
sends the SET_NOTIFICATION_ENABLE that enables all notifications. If
that command fails, it clears ucsi->connector again, unregisters the
ports and frees the connectors.

gaokun_ucsi_usb_notify_ind() takes a non-NULL ucsi->connector to mean
that the connectors exist, and gaokun_ucsi_handle_usb_mode() then
indexes ucsi->connector and sets the orientation of the port. It runs in
the EC notifier thread, which also delivers the completions of UCSI
commands, so a USB event read right after the completion of the failed
command can be handled while ucsi_init() runs its error path: the second
read of ucsi->connector can return NULL, or the connector and its port
can be freed while they are in use.

Check ucsi->ntfy as well, as ucsi_connector_change() does. It is set
only once the notifications are enabled, and the connectors then stay
until ucsi_unregister(). Until then, a USB event is treated as it is while
ucsi->connector is NULL: it is left unacknowledged, or acknowledged
without handling once initialization has failed.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
index 2351da067c5..1998d53e6e1 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
@@ -455,19 +455,32 @@ static bool gaokun_ucsi_init_failed(struct gaokun_ucsi *uec)
 	       !READ_ONCE(uec->ucsi->connector);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Whether the connectors are there to stay. ucsi_init() sets ucsi->connector
+ * before it enables the notifications; if that fails, it clears it again and
+ * frees the connectors. ucsi->ntfy is set only once the notifications are
+ * enabled, and from then on the connectors stay until ucsi_unregister().
+ * ucsi_connector_change() checks ucsi->ntfy for the same reason.
+ */
+static bool gaokun_ucsi_connectors_ready(struct gaokun_ucsi *uec)
+{
+	return READ_ONCE(uec->ucsi->ntfy) & UCSI_ENABLE_NTFY_CONNECTOR_CHANGE &&
+	       READ_ONCE(uec->ucsi->connector);
+}
+
 /* Returns whether a port had an update */
 static bool gaokun_ucsi_usb_notify_ind(struct gaokun_ucsi *uec)
 {
 	int idx;
 
-	if (!READ_ONCE(uec->ucsi->connector)) {
+	if (!gaokun_ucsi_connectors_ready(uec)) {
 		/*
 		 * On some boots the EC repeats a USB event about every 200 ms
 		 * until it is acknowledged. While UCSI is still initializing,
 		 * leave it unacknowledged: the repeat that arrives once the
-		 * connectors exist is handled in full. Once initialization has
-		 * failed, nothing will handle it, and the repeats would go on
-		 * until reboot, waking the system from suspend each time.
+		 * connectors are ready is handled in full. Once initialization
+		 * has failed, nothing will handle it, and the repeats would go
+		 * on until reboot, waking the system from suspend each time.
 		 * Acknowledge it then, without handling the port.
 		 */
 		if (!gaokun_ucsi_init_failed(uec))
